            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "COOK471"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nice addition to cranberry sauce with the raspberries. I use 1/2 cup of Splenda instead of the sugar with being diabetic and it works just fine. I like it a little tart than too sweet and Splenda takes a little less than sugar also. I cook mine for 15 minutes and it does set up nice."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KeenPea7730"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Oh my goodness, this is the best Cranberry Raspberry Compote! It is super easy to make and everyone will think you bought it or spent hours making it!! I used 1 12 oz bag of cranberries and a double pack of raspberries. I added orange zest to the mixture which took the sauce to the next level! I served the compote over Cranberry Brioche French Toast! Definitely will be making this again! I will be freezing the leftover compote in pint mason jars. It would also be an awesome added in an apple pie!!!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-01T19:10:35.861Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TravelOn2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a Thanksgiving family favorite! We've been making it for years with a few small modifications. We double the recipe and use 1C white sugar, 3/4 C packed dark brown sugar, and add about a tsp of vanilla extract. I typically use prepared orange juice concentrate where I only add 2.5 cans of water to the concentrate for extra flavor and then add the required 2 cups to the recipe. I also use a combination of about 1/2 fresh raspberries and 1/2 frozen and save a few extras to decorate. Family and friends alike LOVE this recipe! Recipe will hold for up nicely for up to 10 days after it's made. Perfect compliment for turkey and ice cream alike!",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-27T20:44:53.189Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sylvia Redenius Flahaut"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so delicious. I followed others suggestions and used only 1/2 cup sugar and that was enough for me. So far, I only ate it on vanilla ice cream. Loved it!",
            "datePublished": "2022-11-10T22:28:50.812Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jassell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my husband's absolutely favorite recipe. I have made this one several times, and not only do we eat it alone, but we also serve it on Thanksgiving day, put it on toast, ice cream, even as a cake topping. The sky is the limit with this one. If you don't like it too sweet, I suggest starting with half a cup of sugar. Once you add the cranberries and they burst, try it and start adding more sugar until you feel comfortable with the sweetness.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-01T17:29:21.197Z"
          },
          {
